        "original_id": "4d3bb98c-9ed7-5e04-812e-e4ddfa3cdb60",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Walt Disney, Esther Forbes, Hal Stalmaster\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions, WED Enterprises\n- Works: Johnny Tremain, Disneyland Park, Magic Kingdom\n- Places: Boston, Massachusetts, Anaheim, California\n- Topics: American Revolution, fairy tales, Disney characters\n\nFacts:\n- Esther Forbes wrote the children's novel Johnny Tremain, which won the 1944 Newbery Medal.\n- Johnny Tremain is a 1957 film made by Walt Disney Productions and based on Esther Forbes's novel of the same name.\n- Johnny Tremain retells the years in Boston, Massachusetts, before the outbreak of the American Revolution.\n- Hal Stalmaster, born Harry Lapidus Stalmaster on March 29, 1940, is an American former actor.\n- Hal Stalmaster is known for his lead role in the 1957 Walt Disney film Johnny Tremain.\n- Magic Kingdom was initialized by Walt Disney and designed by WED Enterprises.\n- Magic Kingdom's layout and attractions are based on Disneyland Park in Anaheim, California.\n- Magic Kingdom is dedicated to fairy tales and Disney characters.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
